  "name": "Nunatsiavut Moravian choir and brass (Labrador Inuit church music)",
  "family": "global",
  "lineage": "Church music of the Labrador Inuit of Nunatsiavut, where Moravian missionaries founded Nain in the late eighteenth century and later Hopedale and other stations, and Inuit choirs came to sing chorales and anthems in Inuktitut in four-part harmony. Brass players, represented here by the generic horns card, perform chorales for church festivals, and the repertoire has been documented by Tom Gordon through Memorial University of Newfoundland's Research Centre for Music, Media and Place (MMaP).",
